{
  "title": "Salat of وَ وَاعَدْنَا",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "In each unit, after [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), recite the following verse ([Surah al-A'raf](A11), 7:142):\nوَ وَاعَدْنَا مُوْسٰى ثَلٰثِيْنَ لَيْلَةً وَّ اَتْمَمْنٰهَا بِعَشْرٍ فَتَمَّ مِيْقَاتُ رَبِّهٖۤ اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً\nWA WAA'ADNAA MOOSAA THALAATHEENA LAYLATAN WA ATMAMNAAHAA BI-A'SHRIN FATAMMA MEEQAATU RABBIHEE ARBA'EENA LAYLAH\nAnd We appointed with Moses thirty nights and completed them with ten, so the term of his Lord was completed, forty nights.\nوَ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَخِيْهِ هٰرُوْنَ اخْلُفْنِيْ فِيْ قَوْمِيْ وَ اَصْلِحْ وَ لَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ\nWA QAALA MOOSAA LI-AKHEEHI HAAROONAKH-LUFNEE FEE QAWMEE WA ASLIH WA LAA TATTABI' SABEELAL MUFSIDEEN\nAnd Moses said to his brother Aaron: Take my place among my people, and act righteously, and do not follow the way of the corrupters.",
  "merits": "During the first ten nights of Dhu'l-Hijjah, it is highly recommended to offer a two-unit prayer between Maghrib and Isha prayers, reciting in each unit Surah al-Fatihah, Surah al-Tawhid, and the verse of Wa Wa'adna (7:142)."
}
